  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Showers and thunderstorms at times for Thursday \nthrough Saturday. \n\nA warm front will track north into the area on Thursday, bringing \nthe potential for showers and thunderstorms along with it. Current \nplacement of the front drapes it over the BUF forecast area from \nwest to east as its associated sfc low tracks along the boundary. \nWith this scenario the area will have better potential for showers \nfor the entire day on Thursday. If the warm front pushes farther \nnorth, then there will be increased potential for a break in the \nshowers. South of the warm front, further into the warm sector of \nthe system, increased instability will provide a better chance for \nthunderstorms. A shortwave trough tracking across the WNY area on \nThursday afternoon will also provide for additional forcing and the \nbetter potential for thunderstorms overall. Guidance tracks the sfc \nlow across Lake Ontario and the systems cold front will cross the \narea Thursday evening/overnight. There is still timing uncertainty \namong guidance. Showers/storms should push out of the area behind \nthe passing front. \n\nFor Friday, a passing shortwave trough during peak heating will \nbring the potential for another batch of showers and thunderstorms \nacross most of the area. \n\nLatest guidance is still uncertain on the shower/storm potential for \nSaturday, but some guidance does bring at least a few showers/storms \ninto the southern portions of the area. Potential for showers/storms \nwill be heavily dependent on placement of a shortwave trough \ntracking nearby, with some guidance tracking it farther south away \nfrom the area, resulting in lower potential for showers/storms.",
